it Records in the 1990s was more than a label it was a full blown movement led by Master P that reshaped hip-hop from the ground up. With its unapologetic Southern sound, independent hustle, and iconic Pen &amp; Pixel album covers, No Limit flooded the streets with music and dominated the culture at a pace no one had seen before. The roster was stacked with personalities and star power, and that reach expanded even further when Snoop Dogg joined the label in the late ’90s, bringing West Coast legacy and mainstream visibility to the No Limit brand. Alongside Snoop, Mystikal became one of the label’s most explosive stars, delivering raw energy, aggressive delivery, and chart topping records that pushed No Limit to national dominance. Together, Snoop Dogg and Mystikal showed the label’s unique ability to blend regional sounds into one unstoppable force. No Limit wasn’t just Southern rap it was a nationwide takeover that proved ownership, volume, and belief in your vision could change the rules of the music industry forever.</span></div></span><div class="html-div xdj266r x14z9mp xat24cr x1lziwak xexx8yu xyri2b x18d9i69 x1c1uobl x9f619 xjbqb8w x78zum5 x15mokao x1ga7v0g x16uus16 xbiv7yw x1uhb9sk x1plvlek xryxfnj x1c4vz4f x2lah0s x1q0g3np xqjyukv x6s0dn4 x1oa3qoh x1nhvcw1"></div></div></div></div></div><div class="html-div x14z9mp x1lziwak xexx8yu xyri2b x18d9i69 x1c1uobl x9f619 x82snj4 xjbqb8w x78zum5 x15mokao x1ga7v0g x16uus16 xbiv7yw x1xmf6yo x1e56ztr x1n2onr6 x1plvlek xryxfnj x1c4vz4f x2lah0s xdt5ytf xqjyukv x1qjc9v5 x1oa3qoh xl56j7k" style="--x-minHeight:40px"><button class="_abl-" type="button"><div class="_abm0"><svg aria-label="Load more comments" class="x1lliihq x1n2onr6 x5n08af" fill="currentColor" height="24" role="img" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24"><title>Load more comments</title><circle cx="12.001" cy="12.005" fill="none" r="10.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2"></circle><line fill="none" stroke="current